# Applies to every service image, because they all build with backend/ as the
# context so they can install libs/shared.
#
# Docker only reads the .dockerignore at the context root, so the per-service
# files (services/*/.dockerignore) stopped applying the moment the context moved
# up to backend/. Without this, every build uploads every service's .venv —
# tens of thousands of files — and appears to hang on "load build context".

# Virtual environments — reinstalled inside the image
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Secrets must never enter an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not needed at runtime
**/tests
**/dist
**/build
infra
docs
